From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] ddraw: leaving exclusive mode, the desktop mode comes back before the swapchain

SetCooperativeLevel(NORMAL) without RestoreDisplayMode (DOSBox, SDL 1.2) made the windowed swapchain first, sized from the still-fullscreen 640x400 mode, then restored the mode: the window's blits fell outside the front buffer and it kept its fullscreen picture. The mode is restored first.
---
diff --git a/dlls/ddraw/ddraw.c b/dlls/ddraw/ddraw.c
index 62f9a6b..5e47d7c 100644
--- a/dlls/ddraw/ddraw.c
+++ b/dlls/ddraw/ddraw.c
@@ -925,6 +925,22 @@ static HRESULT ddraw_set_cooperative_level(struct ddraw *ddraw, HWND window,
     if (cooplevel & DDSCL_MULTITHREADED && !(ddraw->cooperative_level & DDSCL_MULTITHREADED))
         wined3d_device_set_multithreaded(ddraw->wined3d_device);
 
+#ifndef SG_MUTANT_DDRAW_MODE_AFTER_SWAPCHAIN
+    /* Stained Glass OS: leaving exclusive mode, the desktop's display mode
+     * comes back before the swapchain is made again: it is sized from the
+     * current mode. DOSBox (SDL 1.2) goes back to a window with
+     * SetCooperativeLevel(NORMAL) alone, no RestoreDisplayMode; its windowed
+     * front buffer was made 640x400 (the full-screen mode), its blits to the
+     * window's place on the desktop fell outside it, and the window kept its
+     * full-screen picture. */
+    if (!(cooplevel & DDSCL_EXCLUSIVE) && (ddraw->cooperative_level & DDSCL_EXCLUSIVE) && restore_mode_on_normal)
+    {
+        if (FAILED(ddraw7_RestoreDisplayMode(&ddraw->IDirectDraw7_iface)))
+            ERR("RestoreDisplayMode failed\n");
+        restore_mode_on_normal = FALSE;
+    }
+#endif
+
     if (ddraw->wined3d_swapchain)
     {
         if (!(ddraw->flags & DDRAW_NO3D))
